1
00:00:07,929 --> 00:00:13,264
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,387 --> 00:00:15,699
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:20,069 --> 00:00:22,720
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:23,633 --> 00:00:29,055
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

5
00:00:29,079 --> 00:00:30,848
Assalam O Alaikum(السلام عليكم), to you all.

6
00:00:33,674 --> 00:00:41,882
We mentioned that Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه), the last Jewish tribe remaining in Madina

7
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:48,980
did participated in the Battle of trench, alongside the Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and Ghatafaan(غطفان).

8
00:00:49,614 --> 00:00:58,790
Now let's go back to a conversation that occurred between Huyaiye Ibn Akhtab(حيئ إبن اخطب) and Ka'ab Ibn Asad(كعب ابن اسد),

9
00:00:58,854 --> 00:01:00,647
 who's the head of Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

10
00:01:01,647 --> 00:01:05,091
Huyaiye Ibn Akhtab(حيئ إبن اخطب) belongs to Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير) and we talked about their fate

11
00:01:05,218 --> 00:01:08,296
that they were besieged and then, they left.

12
00:01:08,711 --> 00:01:12,451
They went to Ash-Shaam(ألشام) and some of them went and settled in Khaybar(خيبر).

13
00:01:13,810 --> 00:01:17,623
Huyaiye Ibn Akhtab(حيئ إبن اخطب) was one of those who stayed in Khaybar(خيبر).

14
00:01:18,213 --> 00:01:21,794
And he was carrying on his fight against Rasool Allah ﷺ

15
00:01:21,818 --> 00:01:25,599
and remember that Huyaiye Ibn Akhtab(حيئ إبن اخطب) was the one who,

16
00:01:26,079 --> 00:01:31,687
was discussing with his brother Abu Yasir(ابوياسر) the day Rasool Allah ﷺ arrived in Madina.

17
00:01:32,306 --> 00:01:34,721
And Abu Yasir(ابوياسر) was asking him, is this him?

18
00:01:34,808 --> 00:01:38,705
Meaning is this the Prophet that we have the description of in our books?

19
00:01:39,499 --> 00:01:40,825
Huyaiye(حيئ) said: Yes it's him.

20
00:01:41,087 --> 00:01:42,876
Abu Yasir(ابوياسر) said: Are you sure it's him?

21
00:01:42,916 --> 00:01:44,424
He said: Yes, I'm sure, it's him.

22
00:01:45,048 --> 00:01:47,154
So, Abu Yasir(ابوياسر) said: So what are you going to do?

23
00:01:47,264 --> 00:01:49,869
He said: I'm going to be his enemy and until the end of my life.

24
00:01:51,418 --> 00:01:57,975
He knows that he's the Prophet of Allah and he still insists that he will be his enemy, until the end of his life,

25
00:01:59,147 --> 00:02:02,599
and Huyaiye Ibn Akhtab(حيئ إبن اخطب) was true to his promise.

26
00:02:02,891 --> 00:02:07,924
So, he goes to Ka'ab Ibn Asad(كعب ابن اسد) the head of Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

27
00:02:08,289 --> 00:02:10,863
When Ka'ab Ibn Asad(كعب ابن اسد) sees him approaching.

28
00:02:11,271 --> 00:02:15,078
He locks his gates, remember these Jews used to live in fortresses.

29
00:02:15,737 --> 00:02:17,884
So, he locks the gates of his fortress.

30
00:02:18,418 --> 00:02:22,065
So, Huyaiye Ibn Akhtab(حيئ إبن اخطب) knocks the door and says, "open for me, Damn you."

31
00:02:22,534 --> 00:02:27,585
So Ka'ab(كعب) said: Damn you Huaiye(حيئ), You're an evil man and you'd bring misfortune.

32
00:02:28,289 --> 00:02:32,562
I've made a pact with Muhammad(محمد) and I'm not going to break my agreement with him.

33
00:02:33,086 --> 00:02:36,869
I've never found him to be anything but trustworthy and truthful.

34
00:02:38,426 --> 00:02:40,092
Ka'ab(كعب) was telling Huaiye(حيئ) just leave.

35
00:02:40,354 --> 00:02:43,918
We have a pact with Muhammadﷺ and we're going to stick to it.

36
00:02:45,098 --> 00:02:48,047
Huaiye(حيئ) said: Damn you open, so that I could talk to you.

37
00:02:49,174 --> 00:02:50,413
Ka'ab(كعب) said: I will not.

38
00:02:51,479 --> 00:02:54,387
Then Huaiye(حيئ) insulted Ka'ab(كعب)

39
00:02:54,903 --> 00:02:58,063
and said: I swear the reason why you're locking me out

40
00:02:58,103 --> 00:03:02,098
is that you are scared that I would share your dinner with you.

41
00:03:02,907 --> 00:03:06,360
So, this embarrassed Ka'ab(كعب), and he opened the door.

42
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:13,805
Huaiye(حيئ) came in and he said: I bring you glory of all time, and a sea of goodness.

43
00:03:15,025 --> 00:03:16,393
Ka'ab(كعب) said: What are you talking about?

44
00:03:16,488 --> 00:03:21,557
He said: I bring you Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) with their chieftains and their nobles,

45
00:03:22,176 --> 00:03:26,544
whom I have left, encamped at the confluence of the streams at Roma(روما),

46
00:03:27,068 --> 00:03:30,398
along with Ghatafaan(غطفان) with their chiefs and nobles,

47
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:34,380
whom I have positioned at them at Naema(نعمه), near Uhud(أحَد).

48
00:03:34,951 --> 00:03:40,553
They have made a treaty that they will not leave until we completely destroy Muhammad(محمد) and those with him.

49
00:03:41,529 --> 00:03:42,631
Ka'ab(كعب) responded back,

50
00:03:42,866 --> 00:03:49,072
he said: What you bring me, I swear by Allah is shame forever and a cloud that has lost its rain.

51
00:03:49,437 --> 00:03:52,586
So, it's thundering and lightning and there's nothing in it.

52
00:03:53,011 --> 00:03:56,666
Damn you, Huaiye(حيئ), Leave me to maintain my pact with him.

53
00:03:56,857 --> 00:04:00,151
I have never found Muhammad(محمد) to be anything but trustworthy and honest.

54
00:04:01,958 --> 00:04:07,678
So, Ka'ab(كعب) was responding to what Huaiye(حيئ) said, I bring you glory of all time and a sea of goodness.

55
00:04:07,718 --> 00:04:14,434
He said: You bring me nothing but dishonor, you bring me nothing but shame forever.

56
00:04:14,851 --> 00:04:20,696
And this sea of goodness that you're talking about is nothing but the cloud that has lost its rain.

57
00:04:21,029 --> 00:04:25,446
So, it's making noise thunders and there's lightning coming out of it, but there's no rain in it.

58
00:04:25,994 --> 00:04:27,317
So it's just show.

59
00:04:29,196 --> 00:04:32,047
Huaiye(حيئ) wouldn't take no for an answer.

60
00:04:32,547 --> 00:04:34,439
He kept on badgering Ka'ab(كعب),

61
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:40,403
until he was able to convince him, to break his agreement with Muhammadﷺ.

62
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:46,105
That shows you the insistence of this Imam(امام) of evil, Huyaiye Ibn Akhtab(حيئ إبن اخطب).

63
00:04:47,245 --> 00:04:50,107
Now, the Battle of the trench was over.

64
00:04:50,559 --> 00:04:58,213
Rasool Allah ﷺ heads back home, and he takes off his armor, and he takes a bath.

65
00:04:59,458 --> 00:05:01,800
Ayeshaرضي الله عنها said, in Al-Bukhari(البخاري).

66
00:05:02,688 --> 00:05:05,804
When the prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم returned from the trench.

67
00:05:05,942 --> 00:05:08,956
And he had put down his arms and taken a bath.

68
00:05:09,448 --> 00:05:11,285
Jibreel(جبريل) came to him and said;

69
00:05:11,685 --> 00:05:17,231
So you have put down your arms, we've not done so I swear by Allah.

70
00:05:17,501 --> 00:05:18,861
Go forth to them.

71
00:05:19,611 --> 00:05:21,456
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Where to?

72
00:05:21,729 --> 00:05:25,699
Jibreel(جبريل) said: Over there and it gestured towards Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

73
00:05:27,569 --> 00:05:33,551
Rasool Allah ﷺ and  the Muslims suffered a lot during the siege of the trench.

74
00:05:33,969 --> 00:05:38,330
They're exhausted, cold, hungry.

75
00:05:39,298 --> 00:05:45,219
And now finally they can take some rest and Jibreel(جبريل) comes to Muhammadﷺ and says:

76
00:05:45,279 --> 00:05:49,926
Put your armor back on, pick up your weapons and go and fight.

77
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:53,250
So, no rest.

78
00:05:54,823 --> 00:05:58,973
Rasool Allah ﷺ felt that the matter was so urgent.

79
00:05:59,330 --> 00:06:01,597
He told the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم;

80
00:06:01,873 --> 00:06:06,610
لَا يُصَلِّيْ اَنَّ اَحَدَكُمُ الْعَصْرْ اِلَّا فِيْ بَنُوْقُرَيْظَهْ

81
00:06:06,997 --> 00:06:09,946
Do not pray Asr(عصر) except at Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

82
00:06:10,749 --> 00:06:12,938
The matter is urgent, you have to leave now.

83
00:06:14,291 --> 00:06:15,613
So, the Sahabah(صحابه) left.

84
00:06:16,344 --> 00:06:18,686
But sunset was approaching.

85
00:06:19,183 --> 00:06:21,465
And they did not reach yet, to Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

86
00:06:22,476 --> 00:06:26,843
So, they discussed the order of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

87
00:06:27,484 --> 00:06:30,420
لَا يُصَلِّيْ اَنَّ اَحَدَكُمُ الْعَصْرْ اِلَّا فِيْ بَنُوْقُرَيْظَهْ

88
00:06:30,487 --> 00:06:32,801
You shouldn't pray Asr(عصر) except at Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

89
00:06:33,323 --> 00:06:37,475
Some of them said that we have to pray Asr(عصر) now because it's already sunset,

90
00:06:37,855 --> 00:06:42,400
and what Rasool Allah ﷺ meant by that statement is that we should rush and hurry up.

91
00:06:43,205 --> 00:06:49,449
The other said: No, we're gonna pray over there, just as Rasool Allah ﷺ said.

92
00:06:50,105 --> 00:06:57,872
So both of them wanted to follow, what they understood to be, the meaning of the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

93
00:06:58,678 --> 00:07:02,953
When they returned and they brought the matter up, to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

94
00:07:02,993 --> 00:07:06,453
he didn't reprimand any one of them, he didn't disapprove anyone.

95
00:07:06,662 --> 00:07:11,419
And this shows you that disagreements in issues of Sharia(شريعة) do occur,

96
00:07:11,577 --> 00:07:14,399
they occurred in the time of Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

97
00:07:14,709 --> 00:07:17,320
And you don't have to have one party necessarily wrong.

98
00:07:17,393 --> 00:07:19,599
See Rasool Allah ﷺ approved both of them,

99
00:07:19,813 --> 00:07:23,502
because they did their best in understanding, what Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted,

100
00:07:23,710 --> 00:07:26,152
and they did it with the best of intentions.

101
00:07:27,656 --> 00:07:32,172
Rasool Allah ﷺ laid siege to Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

102
00:07:32,950 --> 00:07:34,180
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

103
00:07:34,309 --> 00:07:42,627
وَأَنْزَلَ الَّذِينَ ظَاهَرُوهُمْ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ مِنْ صَيَاصِيهِمْ

104
00:07:42,853 --> 00:07:52,095
وَقَذَفَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمُ الرُّعْبَ فَرِيقًا تَقْتُلُونَ وَتَأْسِرُونَ فَرِيقًاَ۝

105
00:07:52,325 --> 00:08:00,376
وَأَوْرَثَكُمْ أَرْضَهُمْ وَدِيَارَهُمْ وَأَمْوَالَهُمْ وَأَرْضًا لَمْ تَطَئُوهَا

106
00:08:00,701 --> 00:08:06,819
وَكَانَ اللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرًاَ۝

107
00:08:07,170 --> 00:08:13,641
"And He brought down those, who supported them among the People of the Scripture, from their fortresses

108
00:08:14,053 --> 00:08:16,401
 and He cast terror into their hearts.

109
00:08:16,796 --> 00:08:21,457
So, that a party, you killed, and you took captive a party,

110
00:08:21,875 --> 00:08:26,129
and He caused you to inherit their land and their homes and their properties

111
00:08:26,424 --> 00:08:28,798
and a land which you have not trodden,

112
00:08:29,139 --> 00:08:32,260
and ever is Allah, overall things competent.

113
00:08:33,564 --> 00:08:39,182
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in this Ayah(آية), which is Surat Ul Ahzaab(سورة الاحزاب) verse, 26 and 27,

114
00:08:39,636 --> 00:08:48,776
that He has brought down the People of the Book from their fortresses, and He cast fear in their hearts.

115
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:56,300
So, Jibreel عليه السّلام was telling Muhammadﷺ, to go to Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

116
00:08:56,677 --> 00:09:02,571
And, which Rasool Allah ﷺ did and we talked about how the Sahabah(صحابه) had an argument on,

117
00:09:02,763 --> 00:09:07,886
whether they should pray before sunset, or whether they should pray at Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه),

118
00:09:08,178 --> 00:09:10,486
and they split.

119
00:09:11,089 --> 00:09:16,162
 Some of them prayed, while some of them waited, until they got there and then they prayed

120
00:09:16,237 --> 00:09:19,099
and when they told Rasool Allah ﷺ about it.

121
00:09:19,473 --> 00:09:23,061
He did not braid any of the two opinions,

122
00:09:23,614 --> 00:09:28,106
which is very important because it shows you that in issues of Fiqh(فقه), for example,

123
00:09:28,417 --> 00:09:30,979
there is room for different interpretations

124
00:09:31,066 --> 00:09:33,901
because we would have different understanding of the text

125
00:09:33,973 --> 00:09:39,433
but the point here is that one should follow the opinion because they believe it to be the truth,

126
00:09:39,473 --> 00:09:45,999
not because it's the more convenient, not because it's the easiest, not it's because it is the easy way out.

127
00:09:46,388 --> 00:09:51,050
No, you do it because this is what you really believe that Allahعَزّوجَلّ wants from you, to do.

128
00:09:52,264 --> 00:09:53,753
That's an important principle.

129
00:09:54,312 --> 00:09:56,797
If one has Ikhlaas(اخلاص), in this regard,

130
00:09:56,837 --> 00:10:03,685
and they choose the opinion based on what they believe is the best Allahعَزّوجَلّ will reward them.

131
00:10:04,406 --> 00:10:09,083
So, they laid siege to Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه) and it lasted about 25 days.

132
00:10:09,577 --> 00:10:12,298
One narration is 25 and anothers 27.

133
00:10:12,947 --> 00:10:14,932
And as we mentioned Allahعَزّوجَلّ said;

134
00:10:14,972 --> 00:10:16,456
 وَقَذَفَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمُ الرُّعْبَ

135
00:10:16,495 --> 00:10:21,740
He cast fear in their hearts and He cast terror in their hearts.

136
00:10:22,282 --> 00:10:25,988
And this is a soldier of Allah that we see comes up again and again

137
00:10:26,058 --> 00:10:28,740
 it happened with Bannu Nadhir(بنونضير), it happened with Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

138
00:10:29,142 --> 00:10:34,421
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ will cast fear in the hearts of the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

139
00:10:35,645 --> 00:10:39,997
So, Ka'ab Ibn Asad(كعب ابن اسد) gathers his people and he says, I'll give you three options.

140
00:10:40,681 --> 00:10:41,874
I'll give you three options.

141
00:10:42,862 --> 00:10:47,061
He said: You are aware of the difficult position in which we find ourselves.

142
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:50,523
I'm offering you three possibilities to choose from.

143
00:10:51,113 --> 00:10:55,737
The first one is to believe in this man, Muhammad(محمد), and to follow him.

144
00:10:56,124 --> 00:11:01,492
By Allah we are now certain that he is a prophet, and the messenger sent by Allah.

145
00:11:02,109 --> 00:11:04,933
He is indeed the one described in our own book.

146
00:11:05,508 --> 00:11:11,252
If you do so, you spare your own lives and protect your children and families.

147
00:11:12,382 --> 00:11:14,023
They objected to this and they said;

148
00:11:14,047 --> 00:11:19,132
"We will never abandon the Old Testament and substitute anything else for it."

149
00:11:20,106 --> 00:11:23,556
So, Ka'ab(كعب) said, Since you refused me this possibility,

150
00:11:24,038 --> 00:11:27,444
I suggest to you that we kill our women and children

151
00:11:27,732 --> 00:11:30,692
and go out to fight Muhammadﷺ and his followers.

152
00:11:31,139 --> 00:11:33,822
If we do so, we can fight much harder.

153
00:11:34,218 --> 00:11:36,896
Since we have no responsibility behind us.

154
00:11:37,472 --> 00:11:40,531
We can fight him, until Allah rules between us.

155
00:11:41,208 --> 00:11:46,120
If we are exterminated, then we will face death without any worry about our offspring.

156
00:11:46,633 --> 00:11:48,915
If, on the other hand, we achieve victory,

157
00:11:49,344 --> 00:11:52,210
we will soon find new women and have new children.

158
00:11:52,897 --> 00:11:56,380
They said: What would be the purpose of our lives?

159
00:11:57,122 --> 00:11:59,296
If we kill these poor women and children?

160
00:11:59,470 --> 00:12:01,010
I mean, what would we live for then?

161
00:12:02,232 --> 00:12:04,708
He said: "If you refuse this also,

162
00:12:04,913 --> 00:12:09,060
the only thing, I can suggest to you is that since tonight is the Sabbath(السابت) night,

163
00:12:09,531 --> 00:12:13,731
it may well be that Muhammad(محمد) and his followers may relax their watch,

164
00:12:14,264 --> 00:12:17,759
thinking that we would not do anything serious on the Sabbath(السابت) night.

165
00:12:18,414 --> 00:12:22,156
Let us then take him by surprise and fight them to the bitter end.

166
00:12:23,169 --> 00:12:25,869
They said: "Do you want to spoil our Sabbath(السابت)

167
00:12:25,952 --> 00:12:29,108
and violate it, in a way that has never been done before

168
00:12:29,426 --> 00:12:33,706
except by those whom you know, and who received the punishment, you know?

169
00:12:34,347 --> 00:12:37,046
And then one of them his name is Nabbash Bin Qais(نباش بن قيس) said;

170
00:12:37,312 --> 00:12:40,073
How do you expect us to take them by surprise

171
00:12:40,165 --> 00:12:43,115
when you can see that they are getting stronger every day

172
00:12:43,872 --> 00:12:47,763
in the early days of the siege, they were in their positions during the day

173
00:12:48,142 --> 00:12:49,767
and retreating at night.

174
00:12:50,319 --> 00:12:53,750
Now we see them into maintaining the siege day and night.

175
00:12:54,260 --> 00:12:56,694
The surprise element is not in our hands.

176
00:12:58,020 --> 00:12:59,888
Ka'ab Ibn Asad(كعب ابن اسد) looked at him and said;

177
00:13:00,075 --> 00:13:04,359
None of you has ever made a firm decision since he was born.

178
00:13:05,645 --> 00:13:08,953
So, they were thinking about surrendering.

179
00:13:10,066 --> 00:13:16,953
They send to Abu Lubabah(ابولبابة), one of the Sahabah(صحابه), and one of their allies in the time of Jahilliya(جاهلية)

180
00:13:17,489 --> 00:13:21,168
and they seek his counsel, what do you think should we surrender or not?

181
00:13:22,202 --> 00:13:25,233
Abu Lubabah(ابولبابة) goes to them and when they asked him the question.

182
00:13:25,607 --> 00:13:27,013
Actually, they meet him.

183
00:13:27,392 --> 00:13:32,273
They came out with their women and children and they were sobbing,

184
