376
00:27:13,684 --> 00:27:17,856
 He said: Do you want to remain as a slave or do you want to be freed and I will marry you.

377
00:27:18,047 --> 00:27:21,012
She preferred remaining in the state of slavery.

378
00:27:21,196 --> 00:27:27,545
So, she was a slave girl that was owned by Rasool Allah ﷺ, until he died.

379
00:27:28,420 --> 00:27:34,623
One of the Sahabah(صحابه) appealed for one of the Jewish men

380
00:27:35,059 --> 00:27:39,823
because this man has done him a favor in the time of Jahilliya(جاهلية).

381
00:27:40,328 --> 00:27:43,413
So, he wanted to pay him, back for that.

382
00:27:44,039 --> 00:27:48,158
And this man, this Sahabi(صحابي) was Thabit Bin Qais(ثابت بن قيس),

383
00:27:48,800 --> 00:27:52,919
he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ to appeal for Az-Zubair Bin Bat'a(الزبير بن باطا).

384
00:27:53,243 --> 00:27:56,160
Now  Az-Zubair Bin Bat'a(الزبير بن باطا) was an old man, who had become blind.

385
00:27:56,765 --> 00:27:58,800
Thabit(ثابت) went to Rasool Allah ﷺ

386
00:27:59,404 --> 00:28:03,335
and asked Rasool Allah ﷺ to spare the life of  Az-Zubair(الزبير )

387
00:28:03,749 --> 00:28:05,241
and Rasool Allah ﷺ agreed,

388
00:28:05,835 --> 00:28:09,089
but then Az-Zubair(الزبير ) told Thabit(ثابت),

389
00:28:09,621 --> 00:28:14,489
what would an old man, who would have no son and no family do with his life.

390
00:28:15,276 --> 00:28:20,828
So, Thabit(ثابت) went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and asked Rasool Ullah to free his wife and his children,

391
00:28:20,891 --> 00:28:22,365
 which Rasool Allah ﷺ did.

392
00:28:23,026 --> 00:28:24,300
But then Az-Zubair (الزبير ) said;

393
00:28:24,725 --> 00:28:28,594
What's to become a household in Hijaz(حجاز) that has no property?

394
00:28:29,022 --> 00:28:30,396
How could they survive?

395
00:28:30,761 --> 00:28:33,629
We're in the desert, how would I live without my property?

396
00:28:34,265 --> 00:28:38,831
So, Thabit(ثابت) goes to Rasool Allah ﷺ and asks for the property of this man to be released,

397
00:28:38,887 --> 00:28:40,248
 which Rasool Allah ﷺ did.

398
00:28:40,893 --> 00:28:50,026
So now, Az-Zubair(الزبير ) is free, his wife is free, his children are free and his property is back.

399
00:28:50,813 --> 00:28:53,939
But then Az-Zubair(الزبير ) asked Thabit(ثابت), he said;

400
00:28:54,426 --> 00:28:56,494
What became of Ka'ab Ibn Asad(كعب ابن اسد)

401
00:28:57,352 --> 00:29:01,909
whose face was like a mirror that reflects the faces of the tribes, virgins.?

402
00:29:02,917 --> 00:29:04,616
Thabit(ثابت) said: He has been killed.

403
00:29:05,222 --> 00:29:05,871
Az-Zubair (الزبير ) said;

404
00:29:05,911 --> 00:29:12,082
 And what of our Vanguard, in the attack, and our protector in fight, Az-Zaal Bin Mua'al(الزال بن شموئل).

405
00:29:12,928 --> 00:29:14,501
Thabit(ثابت) said: He has been killed.

406
00:29:14,998 --> 00:29:17,119
So, what became of the two Council.

407
00:29:17,814 --> 00:29:20,989
He said, They have dispersed and been killed.

408
00:29:21,712 --> 00:29:24,571
Then Az-Zubair(الزبير) said, I asked you then, Thabit(ثابت),

409
00:29:24,936 --> 00:29:29,389
by your obligation to me, to let me join my own people.

410
00:29:29,738 --> 00:29:32,518
 There is no good in life, for me now

411
00:29:32,773 --> 00:29:38,200
that they have gone and I can't stand postponing joining my loved ones,

412
00:29:38,734 --> 00:29:44,546
for so long as it would take, to fill an empty bucket, being born along by a camel.

413
00:29:45,024 --> 00:29:47,398
Az-Zubair(الزبير) said: What's the purpose of living?

414
00:29:47,913 --> 00:29:50,245
If my whole tribe has been exterminated,

415
00:29:51,132 --> 00:29:54,997
so this man was so attached to his people, he didn't want to live without them.

416
00:29:55,634 --> 00:30:03,258
And he was asking Thabit(ثابت) to pay back his favor to him, by making him join his loved ones.

417
00:30:03,971 --> 00:30:08,097
So when, Az-Zubair(الزبير ) said that, that was his wish.

418
00:30:08,811 --> 00:30:11,549
Thabit Bin Qais(ثابت بن قيس) went over time and cut off his head.

419
00:30:12,740 --> 00:30:17,499
When the news of this reached to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), when he heard the statement of Az-Zubair(الزبير),

420
00:30:18,144 --> 00:30:20,053
he said, I want to join my loved ones.

421
00:30:20,077 --> 00:30:26,109
Abu Bakr As-Siddiq رضي الله عنه said: He'll meet them by Allah, in the fire of hell,

422
00:30:26,290 --> 00:30:27,885
where he will dwell forever.

423
00:30:28,396 --> 00:30:32,146
You want to join your people, Al-Yahood(اليهود), who died on Kuffr(كفر), fine you'll join them,

424
00:30:32,305 --> 00:30:33,922
but will join them in hellfire.

425
00:30:34,558 --> 00:30:38,084
Again, the men were killed and the property was divided.

426
00:30:38,795 --> 00:30:39,938
Ibn Is'haaq(إبن اسحاق) said;

427
00:30:40,476 --> 00:30:45,134
He narrates how the one, fifth was disposed of because this was a war.

428
00:30:45,198 --> 00:30:50,457
 So, four, fifth of the Ghanimah(غنيمة) was divided amongst the fighters.

429
00:30:50,898 --> 00:30:53,773
And the remaining one, fifth was given to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

430
00:30:53,813 --> 00:30:55,679
And this is how, he used it.

431
00:30:56,465 --> 00:31:01,273
Ibn Is'haaq(ابن اسحاق) said: The messenger of Allah dispatched, Saeed Bin Zaid(سعيد بن زيد)

432
00:31:01,770 --> 00:31:04,505
with the captives taken from Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه) to Najd(نجد),

433
00:31:05,066 --> 00:31:08,156
where he sold them in exchange for horses and weapons.

434
00:31:08,885 --> 00:31:12,849
The Messenger of Allah had chosen for himself one of their women Rayhana(ريحانه),

435
00:31:13,340 --> 00:31:15,859
he stayed intimate with her, until he died.

436
00:31:16,176 --> 00:31:18,917
She still being at that time in his household,

437
00:31:19,115 --> 00:31:23,680
the Messenger of Allah had suggested that she accept Islam but she had refused.

438
00:31:24,397 --> 00:31:28,260
Eventually, she did accept Islam and this brought great pleasure to him.

439
00:31:29,040 --> 00:31:34,158
He suggested releasing and marrying her but she chose to continue in slavery,

440
00:31:34,388 --> 00:31:36,545
considering that easier for her.

441
00:31:36,737 --> 00:31:40,003
She remained with him, until the Messenger of Allah died.

442
00:31:40,301 --> 00:31:42,491
So, slavery in Islam.

443
00:31:43,001 --> 00:31:50,412
I mean, Islam has changed many of the rules regarding this institution.

444
00:31:50,650 --> 00:31:53,785
To the extent that here you have a person who chooses

445
00:31:54,089 --> 00:31:57,998
to remain as a slave, rather than be freed.

446
00:31:58,635 --> 00:32:02,262
Some lessons, from this Ghazwa(غزوة).

447
00:32:02,865 --> 00:32:05,112
Why was the punishment so severe?

448
00:32:06,354 --> 00:32:11,513
Why were 400 to 900 men slaughtered,

449
00:32:12,941 --> 00:32:17,692
and the entire remaining population of women and children enslaved

450
00:32:18,735 --> 00:32:22,167
and the whole wealth taken as booty, why.?

451
00:32:22,598 --> 00:32:25,023
Why such a severe punishment.?

452
00:32:25,549 --> 00:32:28,144
We can answer in one word, and that is,

453
00:32:28,398 --> 00:32:29,231
"TREASON".

454
00:32:29,601 --> 00:32:35,773
Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه) were the citizens of the Islamic State and they committed treason

455
00:32:36,435 --> 00:32:43,477
and it's an accepted rule, that the punishment should be befitting of the crime.

456
00:32:44,114 --> 00:32:47,058
The punishment should be proportionate, to the crime.

457
00:32:47,936 --> 00:32:52,605
And since this crime is so great, they have committed treason against the Muslims.

458
00:32:53,431 --> 00:32:56,749
They have committed treason against the Messenger of Allah.

459
00:32:57,247 --> 00:33:00,978
Here we're dealing with the Messenger of Allah, we're dealing with Muhammadﷺ,

460
00:33:01,018 --> 00:33:02,527
you lie to Muhammad(محمد),

461
00:33:02,947 --> 00:33:04,790
you betray Muhammadﷺ,

462
00:33:04,830 --> 00:33:08,328
you know, we're not dealing with particular head of state or a king.

463
00:33:09,376 --> 00:33:13,847
We're dealing with Muhammadﷺ, he was the head of state, the messenger, the Seal of Prophets,

464
00:33:14,378 --> 00:33:17,290
the most beloved of the creation of Allah to Allah

465
00:33:17,644 --> 00:33:22,765
and they betray him, they lie to him, they conspire against him.

466
00:33:23,354 --> 00:33:28,129
So, the punishment can be no less than what Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ) chose.

467
00:33:28,516 --> 00:33:30,840
And that's why Rasool Allah ﷺ was happy with it.

468
00:33:30,944 --> 00:33:36,033
And he said that this was the rule of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, from above seven heavens.

469
00:33:37,110 --> 00:33:41,090
Ibn Kathir(ابن كثير) said: All that was due to their disbelief,

470
00:33:41,696 --> 00:33:45,470
their breaking of pacts between themselves and the Messenger of Allah.

471
00:33:45,982 --> 00:33:49,401
And they're allying themselves with the clans against him.

472
00:33:49,583 --> 00:33:51,986
None of that did them any good,

473
00:33:52,207 --> 00:33:56,102
and brought the Wrath of Allah and His Messenger down upon them,

474
00:33:56,583 --> 00:34:00,216
a bad bargain for them in this world and the next.

475
00:34:01,184 --> 00:34:06,681
So, they received the punishment that, they deserved.

476
00:34:07,214 --> 00:34:10,735
Next lesson, Sa'ad(سعد) refused to be lenient in his ruling,

477
00:34:11,640 --> 00:34:15,732
because he knew that leniency in such matters is weakness.

478
00:34:16,086 --> 00:34:19,389
It's not a sign of mercy or compassion, it's a sign of weakness.

479
00:34:20,182 --> 00:34:22,892
And in such situations, the only medicine is to be firm.

480
00:34:23,286 --> 00:34:26,311
So, the perception that some Muslims have that

481
00:34:26,524 --> 00:34:32,745
Muslims should be lenient with their enemies, so that we don't want to give Islam a bad image.

482
00:34:32,863 --> 00:34:35,825
We want people to say that we are tolerant and peaceful.

483
00:34:36,183 --> 00:34:39,451
We don't want them to say that Muslims are terrorists.

484
00:34:39,931 --> 00:34:42,036
This is a sign of weakness and failure.

485
00:34:42,480 --> 00:34:45,757
We can see today some of the Muslim leaders speaking soft words

486
00:34:45,789 --> 00:34:49,061
But that only adds to their aggressiveness and the arrogance of the enemy.

487
00:34:49,355 --> 00:34:52,088
So, sometimes the sword needs to be used,

488
00:34:52,349 --> 00:34:54,976
and sometimes the word of wisdom needs to be used.

489
00:34:55,124 --> 00:34:59,920
So, one needs to use the right instrument, the right time.

490
00:35:00,245 --> 00:35:03,054
Sometimes the pen sometimes, it's the sword,

491
00:35:03,450 --> 00:35:09,063
sometimes it's a Muo'ezza(موضة) of Qur'an and sometimes it is the Sultaan(سلطان).

492
00:35:09,629 --> 00:35:11,923
The authority of the Islamic Khalifah(خليفه).

493
00:35:11,963 --> 00:35:13,060
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) says;

494
00:35:13,106 --> 00:35:15,292
اِنَّ الله يَزْعَ بِالْسُلْطَانْ مَالَا يَزْع بِالْقُرآنْ

495
00:35:15,604 --> 00:35:23,610
Sometimes Allah can fulfill some of the objectives of the religion through the Sultan(سلطان) through the Muslim authority

496
00:35:23,843 --> 00:35:26,039
that cannot be fulfilled through the Qur'an.

497
00:35:26,626 --> 00:35:28,797
There are some lessons in the statement of Sa'ad(سعد).

498
00:35:29,606 --> 00:35:31,628
The statement that we read, he said;

499
00:35:31,951 --> 00:35:37,527
My Lord, if we are to fight Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) again, spare me now, for that fight.

500
00:35:38,122 --> 00:35:41,047
There are no people I like to fight for Your cause

501
00:35:41,120 --> 00:35:43,749
more than those who have opposed Your messenger,

502
00:35:43,815 --> 00:35:47,044
rejected him and forced him out of his hometown.

503
00:35:47,331 --> 00:35:51,091
Sa'ad(سعد), being the head of one of the tribes of Al-Ansaar(الانصار),

504
00:35:51,636 --> 00:35:55,464
wanted to carry on fighting Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), if there is any fighting left,

505
00:35:56,429 --> 00:35:59,989
we have given Rasool Allah ﷺ a pledge that we will defend him.

506
00:36:00,275 --> 00:36:01,981
And since it was the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

507
00:36:02,041 --> 00:36:04,770
who have driven him out of his home and brought him to Madina,

508
00:36:05,152 --> 00:36:09,235
we're going to fight for the Messenger of Allah, until Allah defeats Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

509
00:36:09,398 --> 00:36:13,991
So, he said, if there's any fighting left, I want to live and be there.

510
00:36:14,499 --> 00:36:15,328
But then he said;

511
00:36:15,559 --> 00:36:19,092
If You have willed, that this encounter between us would be the last.

512
00:36:19,424 --> 00:36:24,180
I pray to You, my Lord to make this wound of mine my way to martyrdom.

513
00:36:25,160 --> 00:36:27,571
So, here he is asking Allah to make him die.

514
00:36:27,992 --> 00:36:30,047
If there's no fighting left with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

515
00:36:30,417 --> 00:36:34,732
this shows us that Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ) has no objective in living,

516
00:36:34,764 --> 00:36:38,444
except to fight the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), to fight Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

517
00:36:38,627 --> 00:36:41,425
He doesn't want to live to cultivate his land,

518
00:36:41,703 --> 00:36:44,182
he doesn't want to live to marry some beautiful women,

519
00:36:44,391 --> 00:36:48,238
he doesn't want to live to, just because of the sake of loving life,

520
00:36:49,369 --> 00:36:52,186
like it is the case with most of mankind

521
00:36:52,352 --> 00:36:54,773
their only attachment to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is their attachment to life,

522
00:36:54,813 --> 00:36:57,376
they might have a miserable life but they still want to live it.

523
00:36:57,980 --> 00:37:01,215
Sa'ad(سعد) wants to live for noble purpose to fight Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

524
00:37:01,477 --> 00:37:04,178
There's no fighting left, then O Allah make me die as a Shaheed(شهيد).

525
00:37:04,745 --> 00:37:05,521
And then he said;

526
00:37:05,622 --> 00:37:10,383
And don't let me die until I see our affair with Quraidha(قريظه) have a happy ending with Islam.

527
00:37:10,606 --> 00:37:12,023
These were his allies.

528
00:37:12,654 --> 00:37:16,001
But now because his alliance is to Rasool Ullah,

529
00:37:16,366 --> 00:37:24,732
he was asking Allah to not make him die, until he sees a happy ending to the affair of Muslims and Bannu Quraidha(بنو قريظه)

530
00:37:24,953 --> 00:37:30,600
 and Subhan Allah(سبحان الله), Allah made him be the person to rule among Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

531
00:37:30,666 --> 00:37:34,391
 If you want to see a happy ending, then you'll be the one to choose it.

532
00:37:34,798 --> 00:37:35,787
Next lesson,

533
00:37:36,049 --> 00:37:40,676
 the Battle of Quraidha(قريظه) is a special Ghazwa(غزوة), for the following reasons.

534
00:37:41,351 --> 00:37:43,666
Number one, it was commanded by Jibreel(جبريل),

535
00:37:44,303 --> 00:37:48,091
Jibreel(جبريل) came to Muhammadﷺ said: Go and fight Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظة).

536
00:37:48,246 --> 00:37:51,348
Number two, Jibreel(جبريل) accompanied the Muslims.

537
00:37:51,443 --> 00:37:53,246
Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) says in Al-Bukhari(البخاري),

538
00:37:53,685 --> 00:37:58,212
It was as though I could see the dust rising in the streets of Bannu Ghanam(بنوغنم),

539
00:37:58,711 --> 00:38:01,201
due to the marching of Jibreel(جبريل)'s troops

540
00:38:01,303 --> 00:38:04,123
when Rasool Allah ﷺ set out against Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظة).

541
00:38:04,347 --> 00:38:07,529
So, Jibreel عليه السّلام went to fight against these Yahood(يهود).

542
00:38:08,063 --> 00:38:09,918
The next reason, why it's special,

543
00:38:10,263 --> 00:38:14,775
the execution of Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظة) was a command from Allah,

544
00:38:15,202 --> 00:38:16,794
delivered on the tongue of Sa'ad(سعد).

545
00:38:17,603 --> 00:38:22,050
So, this was what Allahعَزّوجَلّ wanted, this was the ruling that pleased Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

546
00:38:22,404 --> 00:38:27,129
even though it was a very strict, it was harsh, but this is what Allahعَزّوجَلّ wanted.

547
00:38:28,483 --> 00:38:33,142
And this shows you that, this Ghazwa(غزوة) was a special Ghazwa(غزوة).

548
00:38:33,588 --> 00:38:41,775
And this Ghazwa(غزوة) was a Ghazwa(غزوة), that drove out the last tribe of Yahood(يهود) in Madina.

549
00:38:42,645 --> 00:38:47,073
Some virtues of Sa'ad Ibn Muadh رضي الله عنه, this Special Man, this Sahabi(صحابي).

550
00:38:47,389 --> 00:38:50,451
Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ) was the head of Al-Aos(الأوس).

551
00:38:51,297 --> 00:38:58,668
After the ruling was delivered on the Yahood(يهود) of Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظة),

552
00:38:59,113 --> 00:39:05,466
the injury of Sa'ad(سعد) which was almost entirely healed.

553
00:39:05,832 --> 00:39:11,325
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), it again opened and it caused the death of Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ).

554
00:39:11,383 --> 00:39:13,571
So the Dua(دعا) of Sa'ad(سعد) was fulfilled.

555
00:39:14,493 --> 00:39:17,145
First of all, there was no more fighting with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

556
00:39:17,834 --> 00:39:21,526
Number two, he died as a Shaheed(شهيد) because of his wound.

557
00:39:21,716 --> 00:39:26,098
Number three, he saw a happy ending to the affair of Bannu Quraidha(بنوقريظه).

558
00:39:27,203 --> 00:39:29,140
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

559
00:39:29,283 --> 00:39:30,366
 قُوْمُوْ لِسَيٍّدِكُمْ

560
00:39:30,390 --> 00:39:31,784
Stand up for your master.

561
00:39:31,952 --> 00:39:34,829
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ called him, master

562
00:39:35,254 --> 00:39:40,057
and he's the only man, whom we know that Rasool Allah ﷺ told the Sahaba(صحابه) to stand up for,

563
00:39:40,216 --> 00:39:41,347
that's one of his virtues.

564
00:39:42,254 --> 00:39:48,801
Next, when Rasool Allah ﷺ heard the news of Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ) dying,

565
00:39:49,132 --> 00:39:52,582
he rushed towards him, with the Sahabah(صحابه) and he told them, to come along with him

566
00:39:52,622 --> 00:39:55,981
 and he was walking so fast the shoes of the Sahabah(صحابه) were tearing,

567
00:39:56,412 --> 00:39:58,227
and their garments were falling down.

568
00:39:58,545 --> 00:40:01,814
So, they told Rasool Ullah about it, they complained about it.

569
00:40:01,885 --> 00:40:04,155
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I want to go there.

570
00:40:04,362 --> 00:40:05,205
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

571
00:40:05,245 --> 00:40:09,015
 اِنِّيْ اَخَافُ اَنْ تَسْبِقنَا اَلْمَلآئكَهْ فَتُغَسِّلُكَ مَا غَسَّلَتْ حَنْظَلَهْ

572
00:40:09,273 --> 00:40:12,118
I'm afraid that the angels will reach there before us.

573
00:40:13,237 --> 00:40:16,398
So, the angels were rushing to go towards Sa'ad(سعد).

574
00:40:16,565 --> 00:40:17,811
 That's another of his virtues.

575
00:40:18,382 --> 00:40:19,181
Another virtue,

576
00:40:19,588 --> 00:40:21,826
when he died, the mother of Sa'ad(سعد) was weeping.

577
00:40:21,890 --> 00:40:23,279
She was mourning on her son,

578
00:40:23,583 --> 00:40:30,179
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Every mourner is exaggerating, except for the mother of Sa'ad(سعد).

579
00:40:30,995 --> 00:40:35,847
You have a reason to cry, you have a reason to mourn, the death of Sa'ad(سعد)

580
00:40:36,276 --> 00:40:38,800
 because he was such a Muslim.

581
00:40:39,621 --> 00:40:41,598
كُلُّ نَائحة تَكْذِبَ اِلَّا اُمُّ سَعْد

582
00:40:41,765 --> 00:40:44,619
When they carried the Janazah(جنازة) of Sa'ad(سعد), it was so light,

583
00:40:45,087 --> 00:40:48,073
so they went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and they said it was so light,

584
00:40:48,157 --> 00:40:50,823
 it was as if, it was empty, his body wasn't there.

585
00:40:51,024 --> 00:40:53,789
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; And why shouldn't it be light

586
00:40:54,125 --> 00:40:58,690
when angels that never came down to Duniyah(دنيا) came down

587
00:40:58,793 --> 00:41:03,399
to participate, in carrying the Janazah(جنازة) of Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ),

588
00:41:04,160 --> 00:41:06,504
Angels who never came down to Duniyah(دنيا)

589
00:41:06,528 --> 00:41:12,935
came down specially to participate in the funeral of Sa'ad Ibn Muadh رضي الله عنه,

590
00:41:13,118 --> 00:41:16,430
and they were carrying his body alongside the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

591
00:41:17,154 --> 00:41:19,433
This is such a great Sahabi(صحابي).

592
00:41:20,213 --> 00:41:24,021
And the greatest, the greatest virtue of all,

593
00:41:24,629 --> 00:41:30,611
a virtue that we didn't hear was attributed to any Sahabi(صحابي) other than him,

594
00:41:31,405 --> 00:41:35,324
was the virtue that was mentioned by Rasool Allah ﷺ in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم).

595
00:41:35,920 --> 00:41:37,279
Rasool Ullah said;

596
00:41:37,667 --> 00:41:41,644
اِهْتَز عَرْشُ الرَّحْمنِ لِمَوْتِ سَعْد اِبن معاذ

597
00:41:42,331 --> 00:41:47,799
The throne of Allah shook Because of the death of Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ).

598
00:41:48,389 --> 00:41:54,468
The throne of Allah, the creator of the universe moved, it was shaking. Why?

599
00:41:54,492 --> 00:41:57,513
Because of the death of Sa'ad Ibn Muadh رضي الله عنه.

600
00:41:58,257 --> 00:42:00,394
This is how great Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ) was.

601
00:42:01,227 --> 00:42:04,037
And some of the scholars say that the reason why the throne of Allah shook

602
00:42:04,439 --> 00:42:08,288
was, because of the commotion that was caused among the angels,

603
00:42:08,328 --> 00:42:11,172
who are carrying the throne of Allah, when they knew that Sa'ad(سعد) died,

604
00:42:11,380 --> 00:42:18,630
commotion sort of occurred and that caused the throne of Allah to shake, رضي الله عن, Sa'ad Ibn Muadh رضي الله عنه.

605
00:42:19,413 --> 00:42:21,455
And Rasool Allah ﷺ never forgot about Sa'ad(سعد).

606
00:42:21,519 --> 00:42:24,577
I mean, even after he died, he was still remember him.

607
00:42:24,998 --> 00:42:27,355
One day Rasool Allah ﷺ received gifts.

608
00:42:28,291 --> 00:42:30,910
He received some pieces of cloth

609
00:42:31,569 --> 00:42:35,347
that the Sahabah(صحابه) never, never saw the likes of those piece of cloth,

610
00:42:35,427 --> 00:42:38,707
 probably they were cloth of silver, garments of silver.

611
00:42:38,970 --> 00:42:41,978
So, the Sahabah(صحابه) were holding this cloth.

612
00:42:42,304 --> 00:42:44,733
Every one of them wanted to touch it and they were testing it,

613
00:42:44,763 --> 00:42:48,027
they wanted to touch this beautiful fabric, they were so impressed with it

614
00:42:48,178 --> 00:42:52,287
and Rasool Allah ﷺ saw this crowd taking look at this piece of cloth.

615
00:42:52,650 --> 00:42:53,271
So, he said;

616
00:42:53,382 --> 00:42:55,982
 اَتَعْجَبُوْنَ مِنْ لِيْنِيْ هَذَهْ

617
00:42:56,334 --> 00:42:59,712
Are you amazed at how soft this cloth is?

618
00:42:59,783 --> 00:43:00,589
 They said; Yes.

619
00:43:00,880 --> 00:43:02,446
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

620
00:43:02,804 --> 00:43:07,792
لَمَا نَادِيْلُ سَعْدْ اِبْنِ مُعَاذْ فِي الْجَنَّةْ’ خَيْرٌ مِّنْهَا وَاَلْيَنْ

621
00:43:08,125 --> 00:43:14,244
The handkerchiefs of Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ) in Jannah(جنة) are softer and better than this cloth,

622
00:43:15,315 --> 00:43:17,805
the handkerchief, not the garment.

623
00:43:18,231 --> 00:43:22,593
The tissues, the handkerchiefs of Sa'ad(سعد) in Jannah(جنة), are better than this.

624
00:43:22,935 --> 00:43:29,775
Now, with all of these virtues of Sa'ad(سعد), with the special status of Sa'ad(سعد),

625
00:43:30,247 --> 00:43:32,458
when they were burying Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ),

626
00:43:33,182 --> 00:43:35,439
when they lowered his body into the grave,

627
00:43:35,836 --> 00:43:37,558
and when they were covering his body.

628
00:43:38,045 --> 00:43:44,078
Rasool Allah ﷺ was standing right on top of the grave, and suddenly his face changed.

629
00:43:44,964 --> 00:43:47,271
And then he said;  Subhan Allah(سبحان الله) three times.

630
00:43:48,301 --> 00:43:51,877
Subhan Allah(سبحان الله), Subhan Allah(سبحان الله), Subhan Allah(سبحان الله).

631
00:43:52,255 --> 00:43:54,759
The Sahabah(صحابه) repeated the Subhan Allah(سبحان الله) after him.

632
00:43:54,817 --> 00:43:59,058
It says that you could hear the voices in Al-Baqiyah(البقيه), in the cemetery,

633
00:43:59,154 --> 00:44:00,301
they were saying Subhan Allah(سبحان الله).

634
00:44:01,152 --> 00:44:04,352
And then the face of Rasool Ullah returned to usual.

635
00:44:04,819 --> 00:44:08,102
And he said, Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر), Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر), Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر).

636
00:44:08,614 --> 00:44:13,307
They asked Rasool Allah ﷺ, why did you say that?

637
00:44:13,602 --> 00:44:16,981
Why did you make Tasbeeh(تسبيح) and then you make Takbeer(تكبير)?

638
00:44:17,567 --> 00:44:18,952
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

639
00:44:19,466 --> 00:44:23,039
تَضَايق عَلَى صَاحِبْكُمُ الْقَبْر، وَضُمَّ ضَمَّ

640
00:44:23,774 --> 00:44:27,285
اِنَّ نَجَّا مِنْهَا اَحَدٌ لَا نَجَا هُوَّ ثُمَّ فُرِّجَ عَنْهَ

641
00:44:27,839 --> 00:44:32,421
The grave squeezed the body of Sa'ad(سعد)

642
00:44:33,325 --> 00:44:38,706
and if there was going to be anyone, who would be spared of that suffering of the squeezing of the grave,

643
00:44:38,786 --> 00:44:40,134
 it would have been Sa'ad(سعد).

644
00:44:40,797 --> 00:44:44,969
And then the grave released, itself.

645
00:44:45,223 --> 00:44:47,153
So the earth released itself,

646
00:44:47,233 --> 00:44:52,038
the earth would squeeze in the body of a person, when he's buried.

647
00:44:52,284 --> 00:44:54,177
And Rasool Allah ﷺ was worried,

648
00:44:54,215 --> 00:44:56,614
when he saw that and he said, Subhan Allah(سبحان الله) and his face changed,

649
00:44:57,267 --> 00:44:58,554
he was feeling sorry for Sa'ad(سعد).

650
00:44:59,283 --> 00:45:02,156
But then when the earth released the body of Sa'ad(سعد),

651
00:45:02,489 --> 00:45:04,418
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر).

652
00:45:04,815 --> 00:45:08,871
So, dear brothers and sisters, we ask Allah, to spare us from the punishment of the grave.

653
00:45:09,383 --> 00:45:13,612
We asked Allahعَزّوجَلّ to make our time in the graves, times of blessing of Naimah(نعمة),

654
00:45:13,637 --> 00:45:17,042
because the righteous servant of Allah will see his place in Jannah(جنة),

655
00:45:17,067 --> 00:45:18,580
we ask Allah, to make us of those.

656
00:45:19,708 --> 00:45:21,367
We ask Allah to spare us from the Fittan(فتن)

657
00:45:21,407 --> 00:45:24,303
 you know, we have the Sakaraat-Ul-Moat(سكرات الموت) and you have the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of Al-Qabr(القبر).

658
00:45:24,765 --> 00:45:27,703
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to save us from all of those.

659
00:45:28,583 --> 00:45:32,554
This was the great Sahabi رضي الله عنه, Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاذ),

660
00:45:32,680 --> 00:45:34,701
he was the head of Al-Aos(الأوس),

661
00:45:35,098 --> 00:45:36,664
how old was he, when he died?

662
00:45:37,045 --> 00:45:38,845
Thirty seven(37) years old.

663
00:45:39,481 --> 00:45:43,197
Meaning that when Rasool Allah made Hijrah(هجرة) he was 30 years old.

664
00:45:43,860 --> 00:45:45,658
He became Muslim before that.

665
00:45:45,682 --> 00:45:52,665
So, here you have a young man giving his prime life to the service of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

666
00:45:52,955 --> 00:45:55,334
until he died for the sake of Islam.

667
00:45:55,779 --> 00:45:57,253
This is the meaning of Nusrah(نصرة),

668
00:45:57,655 --> 00:46:00,368
giving Nusrah(نصرة) to the religion, giving support to the religion.

669
00:46:00,783 --> 00:46:07,888
It's not that you stayed home, laid back, attend the Islamic conferences in the five star hotels,

670
00:46:08,464 --> 00:46:13,945
go to your mosque, comfortable driving in an air conditioned car, in summer,

671
00:46:14,657 --> 00:46:17,053
using the heater, when it's winter,

672
00:46:17,297 --> 00:46:21,402
and then you think that you have done the best that you could do for the religion of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

673
00:46:22,065 --> 00:46:27,741
without suffering a bit, without spending a dime, without shedding a drop of blood.

674
00:46:28,300 --> 00:46:30,272
That wasn't how the Ansaar(الانصار) did it.

675
00:46:30,558 --> 00:46:32,518
That wasn't their understanding of religion.

676
00:46:33,244 --> 00:46:39,861
They spared nothing, for the sake of serving Allahعَزّوجَلّ and His messenger Muhammadﷺ,

677
00:46:40,308 --> 00:46:43,757
and that's why they deserved to be called Al-Ansaar(الانصار).

678
00:46:44,290 --> 00:46:45,602
Dear brothers and sisters;

679
00:46:45,944 --> 00:46:50,516
Rasool Allah ﷺ after the Battle of the trench said;

680
00:46:51,114 --> 00:46:54,542
اَلْآنَ نَغْزُوهُمْ وَلاَ يَغْزُونَنَا

681
00:46:55,400 --> 00:47:00,440
From now on, we will attack them and they will not attack us.

682
00:47:01,537 --> 00:47:08,231
So, the Battle of a trench was a turning point, in the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

683
00:47:08,779 --> 00:47:16,570
It represented the move from the stage of defensive Jihad(جهاد) to the stage of offensive Jihad(جهاد).

684
00:47:17,095 --> 00:47:20,628
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: From now on, they will not attack us,

685
00:47:20,942 --> 00:47:23,172
we will be the ones, who attack them.

686
00:47:24,113 --> 00:47:28,677
So, we are done with the first stage of Madina

687
00:47:29,384 --> 00:47:33,137
and that is the stage of Jihad-Ud-Daffah(جهاد الدفعه),

688
00:47:33,289 --> 00:47:36,143
the defensive fighting Fee-sabeel-Lillah(في سبيل الله).

689
00:47:36,572 --> 00:47:41,815
And the following stage is the stage of offensive Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

690
00:47:42,103 --> 00:47:45,898
we ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to accept from us, our deeds.

691
00:47:46,210 --> 00:47:52,256
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to make us of those, who understand the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ and follow it.

692
00:47:52,755 --> 00:47:57,331
We ask Allah, to make us of those who will give support, Nusrah(نصرة) to His religion.

693
00:47:57,837 --> 00:48:04,123
This is our last session in the first part of Madina.

694
00:48:04,773 --> 00:48:09,186
رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ۝

695
00:48:09,715 --> 00:48:13,670
وَصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

696
00:48:14,338 --> 00:48:17,894
I ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to accept from us, what past from Ramadhan(رمضان)

697
00:48:17,956 --> 00:48:20,876
and we ask Allah to help us, for what is remaining.

698
00:48:21,176 --> 00:48:25,535
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to reward us with Jannah(جنة) and to save us from Hellfire.

699
00:48:25,733 --> 00:48:28,497
وَالسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

